proof.text:
Because $x\in\mathfrak p\subseteq\mathfrak m$, [lem-weil-pbc-depth-drops-by-one] applies to the nonzero finite module $N$ over the Noetherian local ring $R$. It gives $n\ge1$, $Q
e0$, and $\operatorname{depth}_R(Q)=n-1$. It also applies over $S$: $N_{\mathfrak p}
e0$ is finite, multiplication by $x/1$ is injective by step 5, and $x/1\in\mathfrak pS$, the maximal ideal of $S$. Writing $t=\operatorname{depth}_S(N_{\mathfrak p})$, we obtain $t\ge1$, $Q_{\mathfrak p}
e0$, and $\operatorname{depth}_S(Q_{\mathfrak p})=t-1$ under the identification in step 5.
